}

### Ingest pipeline log with full metadata
POST http://localhost:18000/ingest-log
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "payments-api",
    "pipeline": "deploy",
    "environment": "dev",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "build-and-deploy",
    "service_name": "payments-api",
    "text": "Step 7/10: Deploy to cluster\nkubectl apply -f deploy.yaml\nError from server (BadRequest): container \"api\" in pod \"payments-api\" is waiting to start: trying and failing to pull image\nBack-off pulling image \"registry.example.com/payments-api:abc123\""
}

### Ask pipeline log with full metadata
POST http://localhost:18000/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "question": "Why did this deployment fail and what should I check first?",
    "top_k": 5,
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "payments-api",
    "pipeline": "deploy",
    "environment": "dev",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "build-and-deploy",
    "service_name": "payments-api",
    "analysis_mode": "cicd",
    "model_hint": "gpt-4o-mini"
}

### Scenario 1 — CrashLoopBackOff (missing env / config)
POST http://localhost:18000/ingest-log
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "orders-api",
    "pipeline": "deploy",
    "environment": "dev",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "deploy-to-aks",
    "service_name": "orders-api",
    "text": "Step 8/10: Deploy to AKS\nkubectl apply -f deployment.yaml\nDeployment.apps/orders-api configured\nkubectl rollout status deployment/orders-api\nWaiting for deployment \"orders-api\" rollout to finish: 1 out of 2 new replicas have been updated...\npod/orders-api-6d4f7c9b6f-abcde   0/1     CrashLoopBackOff   3 (10s ago)   45s\nkubectl logs orders-api-6d4f7c9b6f-abcde\nError: missing required environment variable DATABASE_URL\nApplication failed to start"
  }

### Scenario 1 — Ask about CrashLoopBackOff
POST http://localhost:18000/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "question": "Why is this deployment failing?",
    "top_k": 5,
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "orders-api",
    "pipeline": "deploy",
    "environment": "dev",
    "status": "failed",
    "analysis_mode": "cicd",
    "model_hint": "gpt-4o-mini"
  }

### Scenario 2 — Terraform apply failure (auth issue)
POST http://localhost:18000/ingest-log
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "infra-live",
    "pipeline": "terraform-apply",
    "environment": "prod",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "terraform",
    "service_name": "aks-cluster",
    "text": "Run terraform apply -auto-approve\nmodule.aks.azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main: Creating...\n\nError: authorization failed\n\nError: building AzureRM Client: obtain subscription() from Azure CLI: parsing json result from the Azure CLI: waiting for the Azure CLI: exit status 1: ERROR: Please run 'az login' to setup account.\n\n\nError: unable to authenticate to Azure provider\n\non provider.tf line 3, in provider \"azurerm\":\n3: provider \"azurerm\" {"
  }

### Scenario 2 — Ask about Terraform apply failure
POST http://localhost:18000/ask
Content-Type: application/json

  {
    "question": "Why did terraform apply fail and what should be fixed?",
    "top_k": 5,
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "infra-live",
    "pipeline": "terraform-apply",
    "environment": "prod",
    "status": "failed",
    "analysis_mode": "cicd",
    "model_hint": "gpt-4o-mini"
  }

### Scenario 3 — GitHub Actions build/push failure (image not found / tag mismatch)
POST http://localhost:18000/ingest-log
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "payments-api",
    "pipeline": "build",
    "environment": "dev",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "docker-build",
    "service_name": "payments-api",
    "text": "Step 5/8: Build Docker image\nSuccessfully built 9f8a1c2\nStep 6/8: Tag image\nTagging image as registry.example.com/payments-api:latest\nStep 7/8: Push image\nThe push refers to repository [registry.example.com/payments-api]\ndenied: requested access to the resource is denied\nError: failed to push image\n\nError: process completed with exit code 1"
  }

### Scenario 3 — Ask about GitHub Actions build/push failure
POST http://localhost:18000/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "question": "Why did the build pipeline fail?",
    "top_k": 5,
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "payments-api",
    "pipeline": "build",
    "environment": "dev",
    "status": "failed",
    "analysis_mode": "cicd",
    "model_hint": "gpt-4o-mini"
  }

### Action workflow logs
POST http://localhost:18000/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "question": "Based on the failure log excerpt, what command failed, what is the immediate root cause, and what should be fixed first?",
    "top_k": 5,
    "min_relevance": 5,
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "cicd-demo",
    "pipeline": "failing-ci",
    "environment": "ci",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "failing-ci",
    "analysis_mode": "cicd",
    "model_hint": "gpt-4o-mini",
    "content_type": "logs",
    "run_id": "23962390227"
  }

### Action workflow ingest log with run id
POST http://localhost:18000/ingest-log
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "cicd-demo",
    "pipeline": "failing-ci",
    "environment": "ci",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "failing-ci",
    "service_name": "demo-app",
    "content_type": "logs",
    "run_id": "23406546568",
    "text": "15:failing-test Run app 2026-03-22T15:43:43.8681669Z SyntaxError: expected ':' \n16:failing-test Run app 2026-03-22T15:43:43.8720320Z ##[error]Process completed with exit code 1."
}

### Check what is ingested
GET http://localhost:18000/ingested?source=github-actions

### Delete ingested logs
DELETE http://localhost:18000/delete_source?source=github-actions

### Suggest fix query
POST http://localhost:18000/suggest-fix
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "question": "Based on this failure, what are the actionable fixes? Provide one primary diagnosis and 1-3 structured fix suggestions with target files, commands, and safety assessment.",
    "top_k": 5,
    "source": "github-actions",
    "repo": "cicd-demo",
    "pipeline": "failing-ci",
    "environment": "ci",
    "status": "failed",
    "workflow": "failing-ci",
    "model_hint": "gpt-4o-mini",
    "apply_mode": false,
    "min_relevance": 2.0,
    "run_id": "23981327892"
  }